  "notes": "First external ingest (GH #88 / RM-2542). Source: nvidia/Open-SWE-Traces @4fa4c2ae9afc6b397bc50391d43450c79993c138 (CC-BY-4.0, card v2.0), config v1.0 (openhands+sweagent x minimax_m25+qwen35_122b, swe-rebench-v2 only). Filter: resolved=1, language in {python,rust}, license in {MIT,Apache-2.0,BSD-2-Clause,BSD-3-Clause} (no exclusions on this axis - all source rows allowlisted), <=3 trajectories/instance_id, non-empty model_patch <96KiB, upstream join to nebius/SWE-rebench-V2 @d7608f017a29 supplies pr_url/base_commit/created_at/problem_statement. Census 151219 rows -> 9051 candidates -> 8020 records (44 dropped over 96KiB patch budget, 987 strict-policy sensitive: 922 user-home paths + 74 secret-looking strings). Curated 300 (150 per language, 1 record/repo, deterministic). outcome=merged describes the reference PR state, not the model patch; resolved=1 is upstream FAIL_TO_PASS evidence. SWE-bench Verified+Lite contamination check: 0 instance_id overlaps; pvlib/pvlib-python repo overlap -> eval_only. Repo-level split sha256(repo.casefold())[:8]%5==0 -> eval. review_signals absent on all records (trajectory distillate, no review evidence). Sidecar carries created_at (real PR-creation instant), never timestamp/merged_at: no merge time exists upstream, so v0->v1 migration refuses all records missing_terminal_timestamp - fail-closed by design. Patches preserved byte-exact (a trailing space-line is hunk-significant). Full per-stage counts: datasets/raw/open-swe-traces/ingest-report.json (raw lane, uncommitted).",
